@@ -58,6 +58,20 @@ In addition, the `md_globals` parameter of
 `Markdown.extensions.Extension.extendMarkdown()` is no longer recognized as a
 valid parameter and will raise an error if provided.
 
+### `UnescapePostprocessor` replaced by `UnescapeTreeprocessor`
+
+Backslash escaped characters are now restored by the new
+`markdown.treeprocessors.UnescapeTreeprocessor`, which runs on the ElementTree
+before serialization, rather than by `markdown.postprocessors.UnescapePostprocessor`,
+which ran on the serialized output. As a result, escaped characters are now
+properly escaped by the serializer like any other text. Previously, when the
+[smarty](../extensions/smarty.md) extension was enabled, an escaped double quote
+(`\"`) in an image's alt text or a link's title would generate invalid HTML.
+Likewise, an escaped `>` in text is now output as `&gt;`.
+
+The `UnescapePostprocessor` is deprecated, is no longer registered by default,
+and will be removed in a future release.
+
 ## New features
 
 The following new features have been included in the 3.4 release:
@@ -97,3 +111,5 @@ The following bug fixes are included in the 3.4 release:
 
 * Extension entry-points are only loaded if needed (#1216).
 * Added additional checks to the `<pre><code>` handling of `PrettifyTreeprocessor` (#1261, #1263).
+* Backslash escaped characters are properly escaped in attributes and text, so
+  that the `smarty` extension no longer generates invalid HTML for `\"`.
